WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.210
COLT MCANLIS: Google
Cloud Next 2017

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.780
hosted a profusion of talks
detailing the future of Cloud.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.000
If you didn't get a chance
to catch the session,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.090
"Google's Identity as a
Service for GCP and G Suite,"

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.488
then stay tuned, because
here's the recap.

00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:16.834
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:21.030
If you operate in a dual
world of on-premise and cloud,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.590
you can use identity
as a service

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.270
to extend your
on-premise identity

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.840
process to your
cloud-based applications.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.370
RETO MEIER: Google's
newly-announced identity

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.340
as a service offering,
Google Cloud Identity,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.470
extends the cloud identity
solution used by G Suite

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.650
to all Google's
cloud-based products.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.020
COLT MCANLIS: You don't have
to be a G Suite customer

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.400
to use cloud identity.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.020
And Cloud Identity
makes managing

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.210
your non-Google
Cloud-based applications

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.001
simple with SSO and central
provisioning for administration

00:00:49.001 --> 00:00:49.500
ease.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.140
RETO MEIER: Cloud Identity
makes identity management

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.570
across your organization
consistent, secure,

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:55.890
and seamless.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.560
To do so, it offers a
comprehensive cloud directory

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.620
that stores your users/groups,
devices, and applications

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.129
they can access, which syncs
with your on-premise directory.

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:07.675
COLT MCANLIS: It also
offers comprehensive access

00:01:07.675 --> 00:01:08.175
management.

00:01:08.175 --> 00:01:11.010
Now, your users work with
a variety of applications,

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.940
both local and cloud-based,
from a variety of organizations,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.400
which means they're more
likely to reuse passwords

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.470
than remember different
ones for each app.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.210
So you can use Cloud
Identity as a way

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.625
to keep things secure
without adding friction.

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.920
RETO MEIER: Finally, you
can use Cloud Identity

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.770
to set the right level of
authorization and access

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:29.470
control.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:32.400
For example, you can require
that access to your payroll app

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.830
requires use of
two-factor authentication

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.830
every time with short
session token durations.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.530
Both static conditions and
runtime dynamic conditions

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.592
are supported.

00:01:41.592 --> 00:01:43.050
COLT MCANLIS: Of
course, everything

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.880
needs to be driven
by open standard,

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.214
so there is never an
issue with vendor lock-in.

00:01:47.214 --> 00:01:49.380
Cloud Identity makes managing
your other cloud-based

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.550
applications simple.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.820
SSO is supported as-is,
provisioning them centrally

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.320
for administration ease.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.090
And if you're an
existing GCP customer,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.670
it's really simple to
onboard enterprise identity

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.580
using Google's ID as a service.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.310
RETO MEIER: What makes Google
a compelling Cloud Identity

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.680
provider is the robust
and secure infrastructure

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.030
that backs the service.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.370
Based on our experience
running seven services

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.280
with a monthly active user
account of over a billion

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.340
users, we apply advanced
machine learning techniques

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.230
to identify threats
and design and build

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.050
custom hardened systems
from hardware, to networks,

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.190
to software.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.810
This is the same
infrastructure that

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.790
supports Google's businesses.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.990
While we don't support
legacy protocols,

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.800
we do work with trusted
partners like Okta and Ping

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.650
to enable an end-to-end
solution for our customers

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.590
that spans cloud and
hybrid-use cases.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.770
Use Google's Cloud Identity and
Directory as your master source

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.080
to get the benefits of
Google's infrastructure

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.270
and use a recommended
partner to help bridge

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:47.920
between cloud and on-premise.

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.430
COLT MCANLIS: In all
cases, keeping your trust

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.390
is paramount.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.460
Your data is always yours,
and Google will never

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.020
use your data for ads.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.470
Cloud Identity meets compliance
and regulatory needs, including

00:02:58.470 --> 00:02:59.610
various certifications.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.599
And we publicly document
security best practices,

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:04.890
including employee background
checks, independent audit

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.840
processes, and more.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.000
To see demos on how
to onboard identities

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.400
to GCP using ID as
a service and how

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.770
Netflix has used Google Identity
to help power their business,

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.340
check out the full
session video on YouTube.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.241
And if you want more recaps
on great Next content,

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:22.240
make sure to check out
the rest of our playlist.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.140
And don't forget the Next
World Tour, coming soon

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.090
to a city near you.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:30.440
[MUSIC PLAYING]

